# Palettes of the HypView icon patch (recolour-cicons.py, TASK/A141).
# Check: (cd sdk/overlays/hypview/rsc && shasum -a 256 -c palettes.sha256)
#
# nvdi.pal: verbatim copy of FreeMiNT's xaaes/src.km/pal/nvdi.pal at commit
#   f906416a9387ed68876c738cfc5c30037b294fc0 (references/freemint, ADR-027),
#   the palette XaAES maps HypView-style icons from (`icn_pal_name = nvdi`,
#   references/freemint/xaaes/src.km/example.cnf:609-630). GPL, as FreeMiNT.
#
# tos-default.pal: the NewTOS default palette, written by
#   python3 sdk/overlays/hypview/rsc/recolour-cicons.py tos-pal \
#       kernel/src/vdi_backend.rs sdk/overlays/hypview/rsc/tos-default.pal
#   from kernel/src/vdi_backend.rs:56@VIDEL_PALETTE1 (pens 0..15) and
#   kernel/src/vdi_backend.rs:69@VIDEL_PALETTE2 (pens 16..255), which are
#   EmuTOS' videl_palette1/videl_palette2 (references/emutos/vdi/vdi_col.c:130-199,
#   EmuTOS 1a7484ab, the same file in the oracle tree). The host test
#   tools/xtask/src/rsc_recolour_tests.rs holds it equal to both.
15b4b326f0b6f05717ec9470fc766019556232f566f3dcccc11901eb1f40cfc5  nvdi.pal
a5ea7f8b3ae0a15a1331bac6fef1394ccbbc57ce083f0f7e5d785e1457682177  tos-default.pal
